WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
An American reporter for The Wall Street

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.936
Journal is waking up in detention

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:05.372
in Russia on charges of espionage.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.273
Evan Gershkovich is a 31 year

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.376
old correspondent based in Moscow.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.710
He was arrested yesterday

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.344
and accused

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:13.079
of trying to steal state secrets

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.181
about a Russian military factory.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.483
Accusations that we should take

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.317
with a grain of salt

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.119
considering where they're coming from.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:19.819
In a statement,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:20.787
the Journal said it

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.855
vehemently denies

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.590
the allegations from the FSB

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.057
and seeks

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.792
the immediate release of our trusted

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.494
and dedicated reporter.

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:28.561
Russia has not arrested

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.296
a reporter on charges like this

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.699
since the Cold War in 1986.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.700
That's the last time

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.734
that an American journalist

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:35.402
was detained

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.269
by Russia

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.570
simply for doing their job

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.506
on charges of espionage.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.707
Few people really know

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.809
what is going to be going through right

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:43.910
now, possibly.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.079
One of them, though, is Trevor Reed.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:46.813
He was released

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.448
last April in a prisoner swap

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.083
after he was detained in Russia

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.385
for 985 days.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.721
Reed is a former Marine.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.056
He had been sentenced to nine years

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.923
in prison in July.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.025
2020 for apparent Lee

00:00:59.059 --> 00:00:59.793
and allegedly

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.194
endangering the life and health

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.595
of Russian police officers

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.630
in an altercation.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.264
Those are charges,

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:04.798
we should note, that

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.633
he has steadfastly denied.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.434
I spoke to Trevor

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.235
Reed last night about the arrest

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.270
of Evan Miscovich

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.540
What goes through your

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.842
mind when you hear that another American,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:16.376
this time

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.310
a journalist

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.646
arrested on espionage charges

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:22.449
has been detained in Russia

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.886
Well, first of all, immediately,

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:30.323
you know, comes to me as is being another

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.624
wrongful detention

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.294
of an American in Russia.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.796
Obviously, those charges sound

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.898
extremely fishy.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.134
Charging a journalist with espionage

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:45.205
And I think that also kind of signals

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.973
the escalation

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.975
that the Russians are taking by taking

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:50.610
a journalist

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.745
and wrongfully detaining them and

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.315
and basically taking them hostage.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.282
You have an experience

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.750
that so few people have

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.185
because to a degree,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.353
you know what he's going through.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.554
Can you just remind us,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.556
what were your first few hours

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:04.591
in detention like?

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.092
What do you imagine that he's

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.127
going through right now?

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.297
The first few hours

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.198
when you're

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.233
wrongfully detained

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.802
or extremely confusing,

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.471
you're in a state of shock.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.673
You're also in a state of denial

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.642
or you're thinking that

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.943
there's
no possible way

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.846
that this is happening to me.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.481
Maybe it's just a nightmare.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.649
Or maybe I'm going to wake up

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.451
and this didn't happen.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.687
And unfortunately for me, that

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:38.057
that kind of, you know, just

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.829
surreal feeling lasted for four,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.830
basically the whole

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.065
almost three years that I was detained.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:46.699
Yeah.

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.433
And when he was

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.269
whenever he was formally arrested,

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:49.936
his own attorney

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.105
wasn't even allowed in the courtroom.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:53.773
You obviously dealt up

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:54.807
close and personal

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.277
with the Russian judicial system.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.545
I guess we'll call it.

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.345
How do you fear that

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.880
he's going to be treated by them?

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.852
There's there's no

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.219
there's no

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.854
question that

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.456
the Russian judicial system is a joke.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.926
It's a facade.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.295
They violate all of their own rules,

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.063
regulations, laws there.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.899
And there's no type of accountability

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.067
for Russian officials

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.036
who who break those laws.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.571
They can basically do anything

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:26.306
that they want.

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.240
And unfortunately,

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.709
they will do whatever they want.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:30.944
Some members of Congress

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.378
have said they think he

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:33.046
they basically

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:33.713
just outright

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.682
called this a hostage situation.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.550
Do you agree with that?

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.286
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.388
I think that it's

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.357
the wrongful

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:45.692
detention is equivalent

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.894
to taking a hostage.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:49.028
They've clearly done this

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.797
for political purposes

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.098
to gain

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.399
some kind of leverage over

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.501
the United States or make

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.170
make an example out of them

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.172
to make a point.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:01.207
Maybe it's like a revenge thing

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:03.009
after you were released

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:03.810
you gave an interview

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.011
with my colleague, Jake Tapper

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.512
and you talked about

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.881
essentially the way you were treated that

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.250
the Russian government

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.884
isn't just operating from the top down,

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.752
you said.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:13.886
Speaking of them, quote,

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:14.520
They have absolutely

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.322
no value of human life.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:17.857
You said that apathy permeates

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.826
every level of Russian government.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:20.627
Everyone who works

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.127
that government

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.062
has absolutely no empathy

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.231
for other humans.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.666
Do you worry that

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.601
that treatment, the way that they treated

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.103
you, has only gotten worse,

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:30.603
the way that they're

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.871
treating Americans now

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:34.540
Absolutely.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.476
I think that

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:39.012
as Russia becomes more desperate due

00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.047
to sanctions,

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.383
their war in Ukraine failings,

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.452
you know, political pressure

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.221
from the United States

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.622
has think that the more desperate

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.858
they get, the more brutal

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.628
and kind of episodic they're going to

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.764
to be regarding,

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:59.632
you know, our citizens there.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:00.300
What does it say to you

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.567
about the state of us?

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:04.470
Russia relations at this point?

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:08.207
I think that this is a perfect example,

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.776
that our relations

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:12.812
have hit an all time low

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.915
Russia hasn't taken

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:16.883
a journalist

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.418
and accuses them of espionage

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:20.687
since the Cold War.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.756
And taking a journalist,

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.191
that kind of

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.327
puts it into perspective for you,

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.829
how desperate the Russians have become.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:31.064
I think

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.065
you know, the next step

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:34.701
after taking our journalists hostage

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.769
there is basically diplomats.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.504
This is the next level.

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.740
And it says something about

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.775
how far they're willing to go

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.543
and how much

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:45.945
they just basically don't care

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:48.081
about their image

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:50.616
in the international theater.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.051
Given you lived through this,

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.854
what's your advice to to his family,

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:56.289
his friends at this point,

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:58.291
his colleagues, as they're watching this

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.195
I would tell them that

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:04.397
they need to prepare themselves for,

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.032
you know, a long fight

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:09.402
and they need to start taking steps

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.203
immediately.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.305
To prepare them for that fight.

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.941
And I would also tell them to be

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:18.111
cautiously optimistic.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.278
You know,

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.948
my family put in

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:23.516
an enormous amount of effort

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.418
and time in order to get me out.

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.353
And that paid off.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:29.789
The Biden administration, President Biden

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.191
agreed to do a prisoner exchange

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.459
and that got me out.

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.595
And that was pretty much

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:37.063
because of what my parents

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:37.864
had done there.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:38.765
Yeah, your parents

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:40.099
I mean, I was at the White House

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.234
the day your parents came out.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.235
It was pouring rain

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:42.702
and they stood up

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:43.469
in front of the White House

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:44.670
because they wanted

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.005
a meeting with President Biden

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.006
to be able to raise you

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.741
to raise your detention.

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:49.175
What do you

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:49.575
what do you think

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.177
President Biden should do in this moment?

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:52.011
What do you want to see from the

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:52.945
US government here?

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.716
I want to see some definite action.

00:06:57.717 --> 00:07:00.386
You know, they're going to have to

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.321
to make some type of agreement

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:03.022
to get them out.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.590
I don't know if that's going to involve

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.826
a prisoner exchange.

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:07.527
Obviously,

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:10.296
there's there's a lot of different things

00:07:10.296 --> 00:07:12.799
that go into those negotiations.

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.667
But I think that

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.968
it's our government's

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.371
duty to do whatever it takes

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:20.106
to get innocent Americans out.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:22.141
And also on that note.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:22.775
I want to thank you,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:25.077
because it's actually a year

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.013
since you asked President Biden

00:07:27.013 --> 00:07:28.714
if he would meet with my parents

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:29.649
at the White House.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.651
Will you be with Lee parents, Mr.

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.084
President,

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.586
while they're here in Washington?

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:35.822
They say the meeting

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.857
I'm going to see if I can get to see them

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:38.391
They're good.

00:07:38.391 --> 00:07:39.692
They're good people.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:41.861
I haven't. We're trying to work that out.

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:44.363
My mom will get really angry with me

00:07:44.363 --> 00:07:45.665
if I don't don't mention

00:07:45.665 --> 00:07:47.667
that and say thank you from all of us.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.068
Well, your parents are amazing.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.571
And that was what any reporter should do,

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:52.538
anything to help

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:56.342
I'm just glad he survived.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:56.843
And he

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:57.710
I noticed the first thing

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.078
when I looked at the interview

00:07:59.078 --> 00:07:59.779
running on the air,

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:01.681
I said he looks healthy now.

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.449
He's so thin.

00:08:03.449 --> 00:08:04.417
When he returned

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:05.651
yeah, well, he lost a lot of weight.

00:08:05.651 --> 00:08:07.186
And I mean, his perspective,

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.287
you know,
we did that interview with Jake.

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.056
He talked about how bad the diet

00:08:10.056 --> 00:08:10.790
was, things,

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.325
small things from

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:15.027
just everyday life in Russian prison

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:15.561
and also talking

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:16.562
about how he just thinks there's

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:17.597
a complete apathy

00:08:17.597 --> 00:08:19.332
and lack of regard for human life

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.132
in Russia,

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:21.501
saying it's not just with Putin, it's

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:22.702
the entire government.

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.003
Just a remarkable moment

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.204
so I'm really glad that Trevor Reid

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:25.771
sat down with us

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.306
and mentally healthy as well.

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:28.441
We're glad that he's doing

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:30.343
whatever to whatever it is going through.

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:33.045
Nice and really now and just powerful.

00:08:33.079 --> 00:08:35.281
Reporter question for the president.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.449
Yeah. Good job.

